arachnid@notdot.net (Nick Johnson) writes:

> I'm running a NetHack server, and I'd like to be able to increase the
> maximum number of concurrently running nethacks so more people can
> play at once - if too many people try to log in, it complains 'too
> many NetHacks running'. Where can I increase this limit?

You didn't mention which platform you run it on, but I suppose it's some
kind of unix-like system.

Edit the /usr/games/nethack script, change the value of MAXNROFPLAYERS
near the top of the file.
The script is generated from sys/unix/nethack.sh at compile time, so you
probably want to edit it there before the next compilation.

